Design decisions for per-replica CMEK (issue #6317):

- Kept the field name replicationLocations rather than adding a new
  "replicas" field; the type changed from []string to
  []PushSecretReplica with a custom UnmarshalJSON that accepts both
  plain location strings (existing metadata keeps parsing) and
  {location, cmekKeyName} objects. sigs.k8s.io/yaml converts YAML to
  JSON first, so encoding/json hooks apply.
- The alias-type trick in UnmarshalJSON is mandatory: decoding into the
  receiver's own type recurses into UnmarshalJSON forever (stack
  overflow caught in tests).
- Automatic+CMEK (cmekKeyName alone) is valid per GCP docs but only
  with a key from the "global" multi-region; validateGlobalCMEKKeyName
  enforces this and points users at per-replica keys for regional keys.
  ForgeCloud's own secrets.go pattern (user-managed + per-location
  regional keys) matches the new structured entries.
- buildReplication now returns (replication, error); the only caller
  (client.go PushSecret create path) propagates it.
- Regional secrets (store.Location != "") never receive replication in
  the create path; the regional update path is untouched.
